"},{"word":"wan","source":"Thesaurus:boring"},{"word":"weaksauce","source":"Thesaurus:boring","tags":["informal"]},{"word":"wooden","source":"Thesaurus:boring"},{"word":"uninteresting","source":"Thesaurus:boring"},{"word":"stodgy","source":"Thesaurus:boring"},{"word":"vapid","source":"Thesaurus:boring"},{"word":"vanilla","source":"Thesaurus:boring"}],"glosses":["Tedious; repetitive and boring."],"id":"5145d658-170e-4a25-b1a3-61df71c9cd3f"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"munchies":{"id":"093f3e35-cdfe-49e3-823f-711770d9ec74","word":"munchies","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"craving for food as a result of use of cannabis","tags":["feminine"],"word":"larica"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"We were given the first name of the host, the address of the apartment and told to bring whatever toys we wanted. Beer and munchies would be on hand.","ref":"1988 May 7, Christopher Wittke, “It Takes Two To Tango”, in Gay Community News, page 8:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[123,131]],"id":"a71ed45f-03e2-44ed-94a5-319878a59cd7"}],"categories":["English slang","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["Food","food"],["snack","snack"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang) Food, especially convenience snack foods."],"glosses":["Food, especially convenience snack foods."],"tags":["plural","plural-normally","slang"],"id":"a630e4f8-04ee-4856-9b28-4a5709190225"},{"examples":[{"text":"I've got the munchies.","bold_text_offsets":[[13,21]],"type":"example","id":"8334187d-eb6b-4dd2-99a7-a68dbc13af3b"},{"text":"I got the munchies, we got the Mary Jane in the Dungeon / Just to let you niggas know in '93, that's how we coming","ref":"1993, “Player’s Ball”, performed by OutKast:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[10,18]],"id":"002a6fcf-b599-4cf4-b004-299edddf2b01"},{"text":"The girl, who has not been publicly identified, sold more than 300 boxes in six hours, her father told ABC 10. Boxes now sell for as much as $5 in parts of the country, so she probably raised more than $1,500. Yes, there’s money in the munchies.","ref":"2018 February 8, Daniel Victor, “A Girl Scout Sold 300 Boxes of Cookies Near a Marijuana Shop”, in New York Times:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[236,244]],"id":"f6079107-bcc2-48f8-ba0d-f9914ed04a74"}],"categories":["English slang","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["Hunger","hunger"],["craving","craving"],["cannabis","cannabis"],["alcohol","alcohol"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang, with the definite article) Hunger, especially a craving for food as a result of cannabis or alcohol consumption."],"glosses":["Hunger, especially a craving for food as a result of cannabis or alcohol consumption."],"tags":["plural","plural-normally","slang"],"raw_tags":["with the definite article"],"id":"9f5f07b2-1c21-420b-bbce-8482090715f4"},{"categories":["English slang"],"links":[["cannabis","cannabis#Noun"],["edible","edible#Noun"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang) cannabis edibles"],"glosses":["cannabis edibles"],"tags":["plural","plural-normally","slang"],"id":"fcc9807c-3501-4d3f-8153-2ba9ef785311"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"municipality":{"id":"2946b977-ba70-45fd-94f0-d1ca1aa0cfd7","word":"municipality","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a district with a government that typically encloses no other governed districts","tags":["masculine"],"word":"município"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a district with a government that typically encloses no other governed districts","tags":["feminine"],"word":"comuna"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the governing body of such a district","tags":["masculine"],"word":"governo municipal"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The U.S. Department of Homeland Security announced on May 29 that Louisville was one of more than 600 municipalities across the U.S. accused of obstructing immigration enforcement. The federal government called these locations “sanctuary jurisdictions,” alleging they were undermining the rule of law. Four Kentucky counties also made the list: Campbell, Franklin, Jefferson and Scott.","ref":"2025 July 22, Connor N. Smith, Mason Brighton, “Louisville drops sanctuary city status after DOJ pressure”, in Spectrum News, archived from the original on 20 Aug 2025:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[102,116]],"id":"2cd5b0a7-669f-4f3d-8d0f-8da89922eb2c"}],"links":[["district","district"],["borough","borough"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A district with a government that typically encloses no other governed districts; a borough, city, or incorporated town or village."],"id":"54a636fe-99d6-4f9c-ba00-af75eca49575"},{"examples":[{"text":"From another point of view, it was a place without a soul. The well-to-do had hearts of stone; the rich were brutally bumptious; the Press, the Municipality, all the public men, were ridiculously, vaingloriously self-satisfied.","ref":"1918, W[illiam] B[abington] Maxwell, chapter XXII, in The Mirror and the Lamp, Indianapolis, Ind.: The Bobbs-Merrill Company, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[144,156]],"id":"8fe3f08e-7972-4f1e-b201-d0bda07ebc41"}],"glosses":["The governing body of such a district."],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"id":"9cec9b64-b716-4c30-8b42-98b12b630d8d"},{"topics":["government","politics"],"categories":["en:Politics"],"links":[["politics","politics"],["administrative","administrative"],["mayors","mayor"],["municipal presidents","municipal president"]],"raw_glosses":["(politics) In the Philippines and in Spanish- and Portuguese-speaking countries, second-level administrative divisions that may house one or more cities or towns whose head of government may be called mayors or, in Mexico, municipal presidents."],"glosses":["In the Philippines and in Spanish- and Portuguese-speaking countries, second-level administrative divisions that may house one or more cities or towns whose head of government may be called mayors or, in Mexico, municipal presidents."],"id":"9d82f7d4-3c4f-4d8a-b10c-9fd806bfcd0e"}],"related":[{"word":"municipal"},{"word":"munificence"},{"word":"munificent"},{"word":"remunerate"},{"word":"remuneration"}],"synonyms":[]},"munch":{"id":"e2a0a313-d21e-4ab9-881a-42ac8f04e77b","word":"munch","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to chew","word":"mastigar ruidosamente"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to eat vigorously","word":"devorar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to eat vigorously","word":"papar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Jim was munching on a biscotti.","bold_text_offsets":[[8,16]],"type":"example","id":"d2700d98-4c30-4084-bd88-ee759bd3e7e7"},{"text":"At work Mr. Burns spies Homer munching complacently on a donut and hisses that each donut Homer shoves into his fat face brings him one donut closer to the poisoned donut Mr. Burns has ordered thrown into the mix as a form of culinary Russian Roulette, only to learn from Smithers that the plant’s lawyers ultimately nixed the poisoned donut plan because “they consider it murder.”","ref":"2012 June 17, Nathan Rabin, “TV: Review: THE SIMPSONS (CLASSIC): “Homer’s Triple Bypass” (season 4, episode 11; originally aired 12/17/1992)”, in The Onion AV Club:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[30,38]],"id":"169128a5-8506-4393-8532-a02da97360d9"}],"links":[["chew","chew"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"raw_glosses":["(often with \"on\") To chew with a grinding, crunching sound, and with the mouth closed."],"glosses":["To chew with a grinding, crunching sound, and with the mouth closed."],"tags":["often"],"raw_tags":["with \"on\""],"id":"5c7b3b38-3f17-40c4-9c66-84908d869d02"},{"examples":[{"text":"Watching old Bill munch his pancakes makes me hungry!","bold_text_offsets":[[18,23]],"type":"example","id":"b5c221d5-7eb6-4325-867d-5b8ba0998412"},{"text":"Think of banking today and the image is of grey-suited men in towering skyscrapers. Its future, however, is being shaped in converted warehouses and funky offices in San Francisco, New York and London, where bright young things in jeans and T-shirts huddle around laptops, sipping lattes or munching on free food.","ref":"2013 August 3, “Revenge of the Nerds”, in The Economist, volume 408, number 8847:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[291,299]],"id":"88178270-1d93-41b7-827c-d567f7fb69b7"}],"links":[["vigorous","vigorous"],["excitement","excitement"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["To eat vigorously or with excitement."],"id":"dfb58d7b-16f1-47a4-96c8-e35df8571e20"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"municipal":{"id":"c68ed896-b87c-4b57-bc27-8a11c54b42c3","word":"municipal","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"pertaining to city","word":"municipal"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"More than 100 provincial and municipal firefighters were brought in, with helicopters and aircraft used to drop water and fire retardant, while bulldozers were digging firebreaks.","ref":"2016 May 4, Nicky Woolf, “Fort McMurray: Canada wildfires force evacuation of oil sands city”, in The Guardian:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[29,38]],"id":"2f873cab-82ff-4536-86cf-73d371f244b7"}],"links":[["municipality","municipality"],["city","city"],["corporation","corporation"],["right","right"],["administering","administering"],["local government","local government"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Of or pertaining to a municipality (a city or a corporation having the right of administering local government)."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"8aebae14-d85a-4079-bda6-29a790972081"},{"links":[["internal","internal"],["affair","affair"],["nation","nation"]],"glosses":["Of or pertaining to the internal affairs of a nation."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"12409d30-23a4-4a63-8f98-5ad359d99faf"}],"related":[{"word":"munificence"},{"word":"munificent"},{"word":"remunerate"},{"word":"remuneration"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"civic"}]},"munchkin":{"id":"cdd33f9a-b68b-470d-bda2-e12b693b0f89","word":"munchkin","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"person of very short stature","tags":["Brazil","feminine","masculine","slang"],"word":"tampinha"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Picture this: your child begins his first day of group childcare, and he is suddenly surrounded by other munchkins his age […]","ref":"2006, Michelle LaRowe, Nanny to the Rescue!: Straight Talk & Super Tips for Parenting in the Early Years, Thomas Nelson, published 2006, →ISBN, page 124:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[105,114]],"id":"30ddb6f7-614d-41fa-b22a-eabba47784b0"}],"categories":["English informal terms","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["child","child"]],"raw_glosses":["(informal) A child."],"glosses":["A child."],"tags":["informal"],"id":"b4ce2492-da6b-4d29-b55e-d6264f58d8be"},{"examples":[{"text":"It'll also have a keyboard configured for a munchkin (...)","ref":"2009 August 25, Jonathan Salem Baskin, “Will Nokia's Next Chapter Be Kitchen Blenders?”, in InformationWeek's Digital Life Weblog:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[44,52]],"id":"f704266c-bd52-4b1e-be75-cfd9029987d8"}],"categories":["English informal terms","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["person","person"],["short","short"],["stature","stature"]],"raw_glosses":["(informal) A person of very short stature."],"glosses":["A person of very short stature."],"tags":["informal"],"id":"013a31b9-e83c-4f01-a5a5-db77d6c0aee3"},{"senseid":["en:cat breed"],"links":[["Munchkin","Munchkin#English"]],"glosses":["Alternative letter-case form of Munchkin (“domestic cat breed”)."],"tags":["alt-of"],"alt_of":[{"word":"Munchkin","extra":"domestic cat breed"}],"id":"409ab5db-43e6-4c6c-81f1-a6f832da8afd"},{"examples":[{"text":"Doesn't anybody recognize humor anymore, or have our faces gone completely stiff from thinking about good vs. evil or character balance or munchkin-zapping?","ref":"1989 October 5, Hwang Tsong-Wen, “Bandwidth Wasters Hall of Fame for rec.games.frp”, in rec.games.frp (Usenet):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[139,147]],"id":"502c9cba-93e3-4e10-8999-7896e497354e"},{"text":"Munchkinism is similar to \"Monty Haul\" gaming; however it involves playing at incredible power levels purely for the sake of watching the terrain get blown away by player characters who are unstoppable. Munchkinism also involves \"rules rape,\" wherein players milk every advantage out of the rules. Often a munchkin will carry a favorite character from game to game, usually with the maximum allowable ability scores, skill ratings, etc - and enough hardware/magic to destroy the planet four times over.","ref":"1993 February 22, Magnus, “What is Munchkinism? What does the Wizard of Oz have to do with roleplaying games?”, in news.answers (Usenet):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[306,314]],"id":"0640c6e6-e49f-43ca-993b-7054a1c34458"},{"text":"younger gamers of a power-oriented mindset .. an immature power-gamer who has +10 Swords of Slay Anything for wallpaper. It derives from those Oz denizines, Munchkins, to young gamers who often go in for hack'n'slash Monty Hauls, to anyone who seems more concerned with Winning (usually by killing anything that stands in his path) than with playing a game with other people.","ref":"1995 June 14, Phil Masters, Elizabeth McCoy, “What does the term 'munchkin' refer to?”, in rec.games.frp.gurps (Usenet):","type":"quotation","id":"d50991d3-de97-4e34-b12e-84ba2d4836a9"},{"text":"You ARE a munchkin if .. you roll 4d6 and keep *all four*","ref":"1997 January 31, Bill Wilson via Wildwood, “For those who are new... The Munchkin File!”, in rec.games.frp.dnd (Usenet):","type":"quotation","id":"b5bf3ba5-9573-408a-9c59-10558ed8a8cd"},{"text":"There are many different answers, but here's mine: A munchkin is someone who's chiefly concerned with \"playing to win\" - which might be quite appropriate in a game of checkers, but can be very annoying in a roleplaying game.","ref":"2001 March 7, \"Caldera OpenLinux User\", “Re: what's a munchkin ?”, in alt.games.baldurs-gate (Usenet):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[53,61]],"id":"0b1cc94a-09b6-43b6-8ade-a066920ac8a3"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Role-playing games"],"links":[["roleplaying game","roleplaying game"],["player","player"],["concentrate","concentrate"],["character","character"],["power","power"],["capabilities","capability"]],"raw_glosses":["(roleplaying games) A player who mainly concentrates on increasing their character's power and capabilities."],"qualifier":"roleplaying games","glosses":["A player who mainly concentrates on increasing their character's power and capabilities."],"id":"cbcec6d1-0633-471f-aa88-3422c9c00fa2"},{"senseid":["en:donut hole"],"categories":["English informal terms","English slang"],"links":[["donut hole","donut hole#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(informal, slang) Synonym of donut hole (“ball-shaped pastry”)."],"glosses":["Synonym of donut hole (“ball-shaped pastry”)."],"tags":["informal","slang"],"synonyms":[{"word":"donut hole","extra":"ball-shaped pastry","tags":["synonym","synonym-of"]}],"id":"9aabb108-fb5e-44f5-be6b-4a48ccd73e56"},{"categories":["English informal terms"],"links":[["pet name","pet name#English"],["adorable","adorable#English"],["pet","pet#English"],["child","child#English"],["romantic partner","romantic partner#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(informal) A pet name one used for someone considered adorable, such as a pet, child, or a romantic partner."],"glosses":["A pet name one used for someone considered adorable, such as a pet, child, or a romantic partner."],"tags":["informal"],"id":"646dd055-f534-4624-9195-b9be16e9581b"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"sense":"child","word":"child"},{"sense":"small person","word":"dwarf"},{"sense":"small person","word":"lilliputian"},{"sense":"small person","word":"pygmy"},{"sense":"small person","word":"tiddler"}]},"munificence":{"id":"760ddc16-6836-49eb-ac48-281c736d5d5c","word":"munificence","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the quality of being munificent; generosity","tags":["feminine"],"word":"munificência"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Now the happy king laid the forehead of thankſgiving upon the duſt of gratitude; he opened the doors of his wealth to the four winds, and enriched the world, at once, with his munificence.","ref":"1769, Firishta, translated by Alexander Dow, Tales translated from the Persian of Inatulla of Delhi, volume I, Dublin: P. and W. Wilson et al., page 3:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[176,187]],"id":"619f5bbf-f321-4434-9a42-7a6475761487"},{"text":"And surely, no form of munificence should entitle to a more grateful and lasting remembrance, than that which promotes the right education of youth;...","ref":"1845, Lydia Sigourney, Scenes in my Native Land, The Great Oak of Geneseo, pages 86–87:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[23,34]],"id":"5f41aa61-bc35-4de1-acb6-b9aa16591075"}],"links":[["munificent","munificent"],["generosity","generosity"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["The quality of being munificent; generosity."],"tags":["uncountable","usually"],"id":"096e897d-e1dc-4c50-ad17-df16bcdb6fe5"}],"related":[{"word":"municipal"},{"word":"municipality"},{"word":"munificent"},{"word":"remunerate"},{"word":"remuneration"}],"synonyms":[]},"Muntenia":{"id":"f2f45f5c-d4b1-464f-a4aa-c8cce7d327c1","word":"Muntenia","trans":[{"lang":"Brazilian Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"region of Romania","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Muntênia"},{"lang":"European Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_cod